 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Audit, Experience, and Compact History
+- Fixed the compact history facade so mapping-backed chat records and turns use the shared history accessors instead of rendering as `Untitled`, blank IDs, or `unknown`.
+- Replaced the manually maintained README test-count badge with a CI-verified badge.
+- Rebuilt the repository-development skill around the current product state, missing workflows, confirmed defects, full testing ladder, real user experience path, and owner-level decisions; removed the obsolete phase-by-phase roadmap references.
+- Added compact-history, README-badge, and skill-freshness regression contracts.
+- No live Gemini request was made for this audit; current provider behavior still requires a deliberate dedicated-account baseline.
+
 ### Public Distribution and Onboarding
 - Added `gemini-mcp-onboarding`: its default command installs/runs cleanly without Gemini credentials, launches the real stdio server, negotiates MCP, and calls the static text manifest; live chat and image examples require `--allow-live-account`
 - Added independently verified local image onboarding artifacts with path-boundary, existence, non-zero-size, MIME, dimensions, and structured verification checks; fixed image saves returned as a single path so they enter the shared artifact model
